nodecode-klipper is a rewrite of TakeshiTGAL's TakeshiTGAL/hermes-plugin-klipper-print-watch:

  https://github.com/TakeshiTGAL/hermes-plugin-klipper-print-watch
  commit 1dd1391c171afd92825ec07a81b1efbaca5c64e0
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 TakeshiTGAL (LICENSE)

Rewritten in Common Lisp against Nodecode's cell contract. What the original
reaches is the same and it is reached the same way: one configured Moonraker
origin, the object query for print stats, virtual SD card, display status,
extruder, bed and webhooks, the file metadata for a slicer time estimate, the
gcode list, the webcam list and still, the print pause/resume/cancel endpoints,
and the same watch diff -- klippy_shutdown, complete, error, paused from
printing only, cancelled, and stalled when the file position, progress and
filename all stand still -- with the same per-print generation so an event is
reported once. The API key still goes to that origin alone, as X-Api-Key.

Left out, and why: Hermes's pre_tool_call approval hook, because Nodecode has
no approval prompt between the model and a tool -- the same guarantee is kept
inside the call instead, as a preview that sends nothing and a `confirm: true`
second call that reads the state, sends the move and reads it again. The cron
job and the script it wrote under the Hermes home are replaced by a worker on
`klipper.watch_minutes` that raises the same events as a standing notice. The
optional vision check (one model call per tick to judge a still) is left out:
this cell saves the still and tells the model where it is. The plugin's skill
is the manual topic `(help :klipper)`, which every request already carries a
line of. Snapshot pruning keeps the newest 20, as the original did, and the
stills and watch state live in this cell's own folder under the Nodecode home
rather than in a plugin data directory.
